# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PILOT CORPUS — language-vocab (the second of the two apps James named on #68)
#
# Read at origin/dev@8228db7. Every DEFINED behaviour cites a line in
# language-vocab's own docs/DESIGN.md; every INFERRED one cites a test method
# that exists in the repo. As with habits, the citation is the point: a reader
# can go and check, and the suite asserts every behaviour cites something.
#
# ⚠️ THIS APP IS A DIFFERENT SHAPE FROM HABITS, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS THE RESULT.
# habits has a full backend and no frontend. vocab has NEITHER: the only route in
# the whole backend is `GET /api/status` — none of MVP 2/3/4's drill or stats
# endpoints exist — and the frontend is the untouched web-template scaffold. What
# does exist is the domain: 37 tests over PinyinGrader, PoolMath, PoolService and
# SeedLoader, and they are excellent.
#
# So do NOT read this corpus's coverage number as a verdict on the app. It is a
# picture of an app that built its hardest part first and has not wired it up,
# which is a perfectly good place to be at PR 3 of 5 — its own delivery plan says
# so (DESIGN.md#delivery-plan: PR 1 ✅, PR 2 ✅, PR 3–5 outstanding).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ═══ DEFINED — the product as docs/DESIGN.md states it ═══
#
# Every noun below is missing from the app, because the frontend is still the
# scaffold's single Home page. The generator refuses each one and names the noun.
# That refusal IS the "defined but not built" report, and nobody maintains it.

behaviour BEH-DRILL-ZHEN "Shown a Chinese word, the learner types the English meaning"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:HanziLarge
  then sees region:PinyinUnderIt
  when fills field:Answer with ?english
  then sees region:Verdict

behaviour BEH-DRILL-ENZH "Shown an English word, the learner types the pinyin"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:EnglishPrompt
  when fills field:Answer with ?pinyin
  then sees region:Verdict

# The line that decides what the app is FOR. Kept as a behaviour rather than a
# contract because it is checkable at the UI: the character is on screen, and the
# answer box does not want it.
behaviour BEH-CHAR-1 "Chinese characters are always displayed and never required as input"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#product-shape
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:HanziLarge
  contract no drill direction ever requires typing a hanzi character

behaviour BEH-TONE-1 "Pinyin is displayed with tone marks and accepted three ways"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A1
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  then sees region:PinyinUnderIt
  contract display uses tone marks (nǐ hǎo)
  contract input accepts tone numbers (ni3 hao3), toneless (ni hao), or tone marks

behaviour BEH-TONE-2 "Tones are graded softly — right syllables with wrong tones is 'almost'"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A2
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  when fills field:Answer with ?toneless
  then sees region:Verdict
  provides region:Verdict.states = correct, almost, wrong
  contract an 'almost' shows the correct tones and makes the card repeat sooner

behaviour BEH-NORMALISE-1 "Grading forgives everything that is not the point"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A7
  actor learner
  contract answers are trimmed and case-folded
  contract an English answer matches ANY accepted gloss
  contract pinyin accepts `v` for `ü` and ignores spacing and apostrophes

behaviour BEH-AUDIO-1 "Every card can be heard in Mandarin"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  when activates button:PlayAudio
  contract audio is browser SpeechSynthesis with a zh-CN voice — no API key, no network call

behaviour BEH-POOL-MVP "The active pool starts at ten words and grows as they are mastered"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-3
  actor learner
  provides pool:Active.bootstrap = first 10 by rank
  provides pool:Active.unlockAt = 3.5
  provides pool:Active.unlockBy = 5
  contract sampling from the active pool is weighted towards weakness

behaviour BEH-STRENGTH-MVP "A word's strength moves with the answer"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#A4
  actor learner
  provides word:Any.strength = 0..5
  contract full credit +1, a miss -1, an 'almost' leaves it unchanged

behaviour BEH-STATS-1 "The stats page shows pool size, per-word strength and accuracy over time"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-4
  actor learner
  when opens page:Stats
  then sees region:PoolSize
  then sees region:StrengthBars
  then sees region:AccuracyOverTime

behaviour BEH-CARD-1 "The card gives instant feedback and moves on with Enter"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-5
  actor learner
  when opens page:Drill
  when fills field:Answer with ?answer
  then sees region:Verdict
  contract feedback is green, amber with the correct tones, or red with the answer
  contract Enter advances to the next card

behaviour BEH-SEEDDATA-1 "HSK1 is seeded from versioned data in the repo"
  source defined docs/DESIGN.md#mvp-1
  actor learner
  contract the seed is versioned JSON in-repo (hanzi, pinyin, accepted glosses, level, frequency rank)
  contract loading it twice changes nothing


# ═══ INFERRED — what the code actually asserts today ═══
#
# From the 37 backend test method names. All four suites are domain-level; there
# is no route test anywhere in the repo, because outside `GET /api/status` there
# are no routes. Each is `review unreviewed` per his #68 decision, and each says
# which documented behaviour it serves — or deliberately does not.

behaviour BEH-GRADE-1 "An answer is graded correct, almost, or wrong"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PinyinGraderTests.cs:Grade_correct
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-TONE-2
  contract the three verdicts are exhaustive

behaviour BEH-GRADE-2 "A toneless answer is reported as toneless, not merely wrong"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PinyinGraderTests.cs:Toneless_answer_reports_flags
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-TONE-2
  contract the result flags that no tones were supplied, distinct from supplying wrong ones

behaviour BEH-GRADE-3 "A wrong tone is reported as tones-provided-but-incorrect"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PinyinGraderTests.cs:Wrong_tone_reports_tones_provided_but_incorrect
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-TONE-2

behaviour BEH-GRADE-4 "The grade carries the canonical form of the answer"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PinyinGraderTests.cs:Result_carries_the_canonical_form
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-CARD-1
  contract the canonical form is what the amber and red feedback display

behaviour BEH-STRENGTH-1 "Strength moves by one and clamps to the 0..5 band"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolMathTests.cs:NextStrength_moves_and_clamps
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-STRENGTH-MVP

behaviour BEH-WEIGHT-1 "Sampling weight favours weakness and never reaches zero"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolMathTests.cs:Weight_favours_weakness_and_stays_positive
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-POOL-MVP
  contract a mastered word still has a positive chance of coming up

behaviour BEH-UNLOCK-1 "Unlocking fires at the threshold and not below it"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolMathTests.cs:ShouldUnlock_true_at_threshold
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-POOL-MVP
  contract out-of-band strengths are clamped before the mean is taken

behaviour BEH-BOOTSTRAP-1 "The pool bootstraps to the first ten by rank, and does so once"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolServiceTests.cs:Bootstrap_creates_first_ten_by_rank
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-POOL-MVP
  contract a second bootstrap changes nothing
  contract fewer than ten available takes all of them

behaviour BEH-UNLOCK-2 "Unlocking adds the next batch by rank and stops when nothing is left"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolServiceTests.cs:TryUnlock_adds_next_batch_by_rank_when_mastered
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-POOL-MVP

behaviour BEH-SEED-1 "Seeding is idempotent and updates changed rows in place"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/SeedLoaderTests.cs:Load_is_idempotent_second_run_changes_nothing
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-SEEDDATA-1
  contract a changed gloss updates the existing row rather than inserting a duplicate

behaviour BEH-SEED-2 "The real HSK1 list is embedded and loads 150 words"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/SeedLoaderTests.cs:Load_the_real_hsk1_list_inserts_150_words
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-SEEDDATA-1

behaviour BEH-SEED-3 "The loader derives normalised pinyin through the grader"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/SeedLoaderTests.cs:Load_derives_normalised_pinyin_via_the_grader
  review unreviewed
  serves BEH-NORMALISE-1
  contract seed data and typed answers are normalised by the same code


# ═══ NO `serves` LINE — surface nothing documented displays ═══
#
# All three are the SAME kind, and it is a kind habits did not produce: code
# built for something docs/DESIGN.md explicitly parked under "Explicitly deferred
# (roadmap, not v1)". That is not waste and it is not a bug — it is a bet on a
# roadmap item, taken early, in a repo whose own delivery plan has not reached
# the UI yet. Whether that bet is still wanted is his call, and the value here is
# that it is now a list rather than a feeling.
#
# ⚠️ Do NOT read this as "delete these". habits produced two unserved behaviours
# that needed opposite fixes; these three need a third answer again.

behaviour BEH-LANG-1 "Every pool operation is scoped to one language"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolServiceTests.cs:Bootstrap_only_touches_the_requested_language
  review unreviewed
  contract bootstrap for one language leaves another language's pool untouched
  contract the loader throws when the language is missing
  asks "DESIGN.md defers other languages but promises the data model is language-tagged from day one. It got more than a column: `language` is a required parameter on all three IPoolService methods, so every drill route in PR 4 has to carry it too. Is language a PARAMETER, or a setting the app is configured with?"
  option "Keep it threaded" "IPoolService.cs:17,24,31 keep `string language`, and the drill routes take it as a path segment or query param. The isolation property stays enforced. Adding Cantonese is then a seed file and a config value, with no signature to change and no migration. Cost: every route, client call and test in PR 4 carries an argument whose only possible value today is `zh`."
  option "Make it ambient" "Drop the parameter; one configured language, resolved from settings or an owner record. VocabItemEntity.cs:14 already defaults Language to \"zh\", so the column and the seed loader's per-language files survive untouched — the roadmap promise DESIGN.md actually makes is kept. The isolation test loses its subject, and language 2 becomes a signature change across the service, the routes and the client."
  recommend "Keep it threaded" "The parameter is not speculative surface — it is the roadmap promise DESIGN.md:36-37 states, made executable. And the moment to pay for it is now, before PR 4 exists: threading it through routes that are not written yet costs one argument each, where retrofitting it later means changing a shipped API and regenerating a client. A6-style single-user apps are also where an ambient global is hardest to unpick, because the assumption gets read into a dozen call sites first."
  against "The isolation test seeds a synthetic \"fr\" that exists nowhere else in the repo — 150 HSK1 entries in one file, one language, zero users asking for a second. So a required argument is being carried on every method and every future route to satisfy a property no caller can exercise, and the test proves the code does what it was written to do rather than anything about the product. \"Other languages\" is under **Explicitly deferred**, and a deferred feature that still shapes today's signatures has not really been deferred. The cheap version is to keep the Language COLUMN — which is all DESIGN.md literally promises — and let the parameter arrive with the second language, when its shape will be known rather than guessed."

behaviour BEH-ITEMTYPE-1 "A vocabulary item has a type, defaulting to word"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/SeedLoaderTests.cs:Load_defaults_item_type_to_word
  review unreviewed
  contract the schema reserves a Sentence type that nothing produces or consumes
  asks "The string `Sentence` occurs exactly twice in this repo: the enum member, and the DESIGN.md line reserving it. No seed entry sets a type, no route exposes one, the frontend has no such field. Does the reservation stay, or does the type arrive with sentence mode?"
  option "Keep the reservation" "VocabItemType.cs keeps `Sentence = 1`. It pins `Word = 0` as the default, so the enum can be extended later without renumbering a persisted column, and it makes DESIGN.md:34-35's second phase legible in the code a reader actually opens."
  option "Drop it until it is built" "The enum becomes `Word = 0` alone. Adding a member back later is one line and no migration, since nothing has ever persisted a 1. The type column, the nullable SeedEntry.Type and the defaulting test all survive — only the unreachable value goes."
  recommend "Keep the reservation" "This is the cheapest kind of reserved surface there is: an enum member costs no route, no client field, no migration and no test, and it is the one place a persisted integer genuinely benefits from being fixed early — `Word = 0` is only guaranteed if nothing renumbers around it. It is also already documented, which is the distinction this corpus is built to draw: reserved-and-written-down is not the same as surface nobody asked for."
  against "You have one other behaviour in this corpus (BEH-LANG-1) making the same bet on the same deferred roadmap, and answering both the same way is how a v1 quietly acquires a v2's shape. `Word = 0` is the C# default for any enum whether or not a second member exists, so the renumbering argument protects against a hazard that only appears once someone adds a value — at which point they can append it. And a reserved member is not free in the way it looks: it is a branch every future `switch` has to handle or deliberately ignore, on a code path nothing can currently reach."

behaviour BEH-DETERMINISM-1 "Selection is deterministic for a given seed"
  source inferred backend/Balenthiran.LanguageVocab.Tests/PoolServiceTests.cs:SelectNext_is_deterministic_for_the_same_seed
  review unreviewed
  contract the same seed picks the same word, so the sampler is testable
  asks "SelectNextAsync takes a required `int seed` and NOTHING calls it outside the tests — the drill API is PR 4 and does not exist. So where the seed comes from in production has never been decided, and it is a user-visible choice, not an implementation detail. Which is it: the client sends a seed, or the server makes one?"
  option "The server generates it per request" "The drill route makes a fresh seed each call. Determinism reverts to what DESIGN.md:66-67 says it is for — unit-testability — and every draw is independent. A refresh gives a different card. Resuming a session mid-way is then a separate feature with its own state, not something the seed gives you."
  option "The client supplies it per session" "The frontend mints a seed when a drill starts and sends it with each draw. The same session replays the same sequence, so a refresh or a reconnect resumes where it was rather than reshuffling. It also makes the sequence reproducible from a bug report. Cost: the seed is now part of the public API contract, and a client that reuses one gets the same word forever."
  recommend "The server generates it per request" "DESIGN.md:66-67 says the determinism exists so the sampler is unit-testable, and that is a claim about the test suite, not a promise to a user. A4 says the picker samples weakness-weighted from the active pool — that is a property of the WEIGHTS, and it holds either way, so the seed is buying nothing the design asks for. Keeping it server-side also keeps the failure mode small: a client that mishandles a seed can pin itself to one word, and that bug is invisible until someone notices they keep seeing 好."
  against "You are deciding this now, in a corpus, for a route that will be written in PR 4 — and the version that is harder to add later is the one being rejected. Making the seed part of the request from day one costs one optional query parameter and no state; retrofitting it means changing a shipped drill endpoint and regenerating the client. Resume-after-refresh on a phone is also not an exotic want for a drill app, and the pinned-to-one-word failure is preventable by advancing the seed per draw rather than by hiding it. There is a third answer this question does not offer: derive the seed from something stable you already have — user plus date — which gives a reproducible day without either a client contract or a decision about session state."
